ROLE: Senior Fullstack Engineer (Node/Express + React TS + lightweight-charts).
GOAL:
1) Make scanner more selective (avoid microcaps/low-price junk).
2) AI picks must be "whale-safe" and only shown as AI if DeepSeek passes a quick backtest on the same symbol (strong confidence gate).
3) Make chart live: candles update in real time smoothly.

CONSTRAINTS / CURRENT:
- Backend: server/real-server.js already scans MEXC, emits detected AI/FT and forecastsBySymbol, SSE event "scheduled_update".
- Frontend: ChartContainer.tsx renders candles and forecast for selected symbol (forecast only when forecastsBySymbol[symbol] exists and source===deepseek).
- We must keep AI/FT concept.
- We use Vite proxy: client calls /api/... and /events relative paths.

IMPLEMENTATION (do actual file edits):

========================================
A) server/real-server.js (PATCH)
========================================
Add these improvements:

A1) Add strict "no junk" filters:
- MIN_PRICE_FT = 0.05
- MIN_PRICE_AI = 0.20
- MIN_QUOTEVOL_FT = 1_000_000
- MIN_QUOTEVOL_AI = 5_000_000
- MAX_SPREAD_FT_PCT = 0.25
- MAX_SPREAD_AI_PCT = 0.08
- DEPTH_BAND_PCT = 0.20  (depth within ±0.2% from mid)
- MIN_DEPTH_FT_USDT = 30_000
- MIN_DEPTH_AI_USDT = 150_000

A2) Use MEXC orderbook depth endpoint to estimate whale safety:
- GET https://api.mexc.com/api/v3/depth?symbol=SYMBOL&limit=20
Compute:
- mid = (bestBid + bestAsk)/2
- spreadPct = ((bestAsk-bestBid)/mid)*100
- depthBidUSDTWithinBand = sum(bidPrice*bidQty) for bids >= mid*(1-DEPTH_BAND_PCT/100)
- depthAskUSDTWithinBand = sum(askPrice*askQty) for asks <= mid*(1+DEPTH_BAND_PCT/100)
Use MIN of bid/ask depth as `depthUSDT` to be conservative.
Reject symbols with non-ASCII, stablecoin-like, etc (keep existing).

A3) AI confidence gate using DeepSeek backtest (cannot be 100%, but very strict):
For AI candidates (after liquidity+stddev+orderbook filters), run backtest:
- fetch 40 last 1m klines from MEXC
- take first 35 candles as context
- actual = last 5 candles (their close values)
- call DeepSeek forecast5 on the 35 context candles (same format you already use)
- compare forecast close[i] vs actual close[i]
- compute meanAbsPctErr and maxAbsPctErr
- PASS if meanAbsPctErr <= 0.15% AND maxAbsPctErr <= 0.30%
Only then tag coin as AI and generate the real future forecast for UI.
If backtest fails OR DeepSeek fails -> DEMOTE to FT (no forecast for this symbol).

A4) Only AI coins have forecastsBySymbol and source must be "deepseek".
If DeepSeek fails, do not write mock as deepseek. Either:
- demote to FT
- or set no forecast
(Prefer demote to FT to keep UI honest.)

A5) Prevent overlapping jobs:
Add global lock `scanInFlight`. If job running, skip.

A6) Add a live candle SSE stream endpoint:
- GET /api/live/stream?symbol=BTCUSDT
- SSE headers, then every 2 seconds:
  - fetch last 2 klines (1m) from MEXC
  - map last candle to { time (sec), open, high, low, close }
  - emit `event: candle_update` with JSON candle
- On close, clear interval
This will drive live candle updates in the frontend.

A7) Ensure /api/live/candles continues to return initial history (50-200 candles), from MEXC.

A8) Make sure detected items include trader fields:
- price, change24hPct, quoteVolume, stdDev, tag, detectedAt, expiresAt
Optionally include: spreadPct and depthUSDT (good for trader view) as extra fields.

IMPORTANT: Keep existing endpoints /api/scheduler/latest and /events scheduled_update.

