Based on the error log, the issue is that you have duplicated code in your scannerStore.ts file.

It looks like the entire logic for the store was accidentally copied and pasted twice inside the same file.

Here is why the errors are happening:

    "The symbol 'useScannerStore' has already been declared": You defined const useScannerStore at the top of the file, and then defined it again at line 62.
    "Multiple exports with the same name 'default'": You have export default somewhere above, and again at line 89.

How to Fix It

Open src/store/scannerStore.ts and ensure the store is defined only once.

You likely have a structure that looks like this (Problem):

TypeScript

// ... imports ...

// --- First copy ---
export const useScannerStore = create(...) => ({ ... });
export default useScannerStore;

// ... lines 60+ ...

// --- Second copy (The Error) ---
export const useScannerStore = create(...) => ({ ... }); // Error here
export default useScannerStore; // Error here

To fix this, delete the duplicate code.

Additionally, it is best practice to stick to Named Exports only. You currently have both export const and export default.
Recommended Code Structure

Your file should look like this:

TypeScript

import { create } from 'zustand';
// ... other imports

interface ScannerState {
  coins: any[]; // replace 'any' with your type
  addDetectedCoin: (c: any) => void;
  // ... other types
}

// 1. Define and Export the store ONCE
export const useScannerStore = create<ScannerState>((set, get) => ({
  coins: [],
  addDetectedCoin: (c) => {
    // your logic here
  },
  // ... rest of your store logic
}));

// 2. Remove the 'export default' line at the bottom.
// Use 'import { useScannerStore } from ...' in your components.

Summary of Changes:

    Delete the duplicate definition of useScannerStore (likely lines 1-60 or lines 62-90). Keep only one version.
    Remove export default useScannerStore; at the bottom of the file (Line 89).
    Update your imports in other files to use curly braces: import { useScannerStore } from './store/scannerStore';.

